  "notes": [
    {"id": "note-101", "patient_id": "pat-1", "provider_id": "prov-1", "days_ago": 62, "text": "S: Owner reports itching around face x1 wk. Eating well.\nO:\n- T 101.6 F, HR 96, RR 24\n- MM pink, CRT <2s\n- Mild facial erythema, no otic d/c\nA: Suspect environmental allergy.\nP:\n- Rx Apoquel 16 mg PO BID x14d, then SID\n- Recheck 4 wk"},
    {"id": "note-102", "patient_id": "pat-3", "provider_id": "prov-1", "days_ago": 14, "text": "S: Cut R front paw on fence this AM. Bleeding stopped.\nO:\n- T 101.9 F, HR 110\n- 3 cm laceration R front metacarpal pad, clean edges\nA: Laceration, R front paw.\nP:\n- Sutured under sedation\n- Rx Cephalexin 500 mg PO BID x10d\n- E-collar, recheck 10-14d"},
    {"id": "note-103", "patient_id": "pat-6", "provider_id": "prov-1", "days_ago": 30, "text": "S: Hx of soft stool x3d after diet change.\nO:\n- T 101.4 F, HR 100\n- BCS 6/9, abdomen soft\nA: Diet-related diarrhea.\nP:\n- Bland diet 5d, transition back slowly\n- Rx metronidazole 250 mg PO BID x5d"},
    {"id": "note-201", "patient_id": "pat-5", "provider_id": "prov-2", "days_ago": 40, "text": "Subjective: Pepper has been sneezing for about a week, with clear nasal discharge and normal appetite. Owner has not noticed any coughing.\nObjective: Temperature was 102.1 F and heart rate 160. There was mild serous nasal discharge bilaterally and the lungs sounded clear on auscultation.\nAssessment: Most consistent with an upper respiratory infection, likely viral.\nPlan: Supportive care at home with humidity and appetite monitoring. The owner will call if the discharge turns green or he stops eating."},
    {"id": "note-202", "patient_id": "pat-2", "provider_id": "prov-2", "days_ago": 9, "text": "Subjective: Miso came in while Dr. Rivera was out because the owner noticed increased thirst and urination over the past two weeks.\nObjective: Blood pressure measured 178 mmHg systolic. Weight was 8.9 lb, down from 9.4 lb at the last visit. Fractious, handled with a towel wrap.\nAssessment: Hypertension secondary to chronic kidney disease is suspected.\nPlan: Started amlodipine 0.625 mg by mouth once daily. Recheck blood pressure in two weeks and repeat the kidney panel at that visit."},
    {"id": "note-104", "patient_id": "pat-7", "provider_id": "prov-2", "days_ago": 42, "text": "S: Hazel has eaten less for 3 days. One episode of vomiting yesterday. Drinking normally.\nO:\n- T 101.2 F, HR 92\n- Mild tartar, soft abdomen, no pain on palpation\n- Weight 27.4 lb\nA: Mild gastritis. Senior bloodwork due in a few weeks.\nP:\n- Bland diet 4d\n- Rx Famotidine 10 mg PO BID x7d\n- Recheck if not eating in 48h"}
  ],
